  "FAQ_BODY": "\n<div class=\"faq-accordion\">\n    <details class=\"faq-details\"><summary class=\"faq-summary\">1. Inventory, Tracking & Tool Checkout</summary><div class=\"faq-content\"><b>Serialized Assets & Consumables:</b> High-value assets get unique inventory IDs (DW-DRILL-001, TW-002) auto-generated by tool class (TW, PD, VT, CT) with serial number tracking (factory SN vs effective internal SN). The <b>Article</b> field records manufacturer part numbers. Consumables are grouped into cards with Min/Max thresholds tracked for proactive ordering.<br><b>Dual-Mode Operator Checkout:</b> Tool checkout is done via an instant dropdown <code>[Select Employee]</code> or live search by name, ID, and initials. Selecting an employee auto-fills their base workstation, post, and initials. A quick <b>+ New Person</b> shortcut is available for adding new employees.</div></details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-details\"><summary class=\"faq-summary\">2. Address Storage, Summary & Label Printing</summary><div class=\"faq-content\"><b>Hierarchical Address Storage:</b> Locations are tied to a <b>Zone → Rack (A–Z) → Shelf (1–20) → Bin (1–50)</b> structure. The smart helper <code>getNextFreeBin()</code> auto-suggests the next available bin on a shelf, preventing address duplicates. Available structure types: Rack, Workbench, Toolbox, A-Frame.<br><b>Smart Location Summary View:</b> Scanning a storage QR code or selecting it in search opens a non-transparent analytical card showing: tooling vs consumables balance (<i>80% Permanent / 20% Consumables</i>), items on maintenance/calibration, low stock, and overdues. Shelf contents are grouped into collapsible accordions (<i>Shelf 1</i>, <i>Shelf 2</i>) with <code>[Expand All / Collapse All]</code> buttons.<br><b>Label Printing & Dropdowns:</b> The location label printing modal (<code>locationLabelModal</code>) supports dropdown selection of the responsible person from the personnel registry, formatted media selection (Avery 5961, bin tag, Brady tape), and interactive sticker preview.</div></details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-details\"><summary class=\"faq-summary\">3. Procurement, Partial Receiving & REQ003 Export</summary><div class=\"faq-content\"><b>Multi-Item Requests & Cart:</b> Purchase requests are formed like a cart by adding multiple line items (name, qty, unit price, reason, link). The table shows a live Grand Total.<br><b>Line-by-Line Partial Receiving & Rejections:</b> Each item in a request is received or rejected individually. An operator can receive 2 out of 5 units ordered today (<code>Ops.receiveOrderItem</code>) — the tool stock automatically increases in the database, and the request moves to <i>Partially Received</i>. Individual lines can be rejected with a logged reason (<code>Ops.rejectOrderItem</code>) without scrapping the entire request.<br><b>Official REQ003 Export (.xlsx):</b> Downloads a filled official expense request form (.xlsx) with items automatically inserted into rows 7, 8, 9 of the corporate template and corrected Sum formulas.</div></details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-details\"><summary class=\"faq-summary\">4. Risks, 5S Audits & Score Breakdown</summary><div class=\"faq-content\"><b>Station | Post Risk Grouping:</b> The risk and incident chart groups equipment by workstations (<i>Assembly | Post 1</i>). Hovering over the bars displays a tooltip with the Program, Station, Post, Responsible Employee, and detailed rating factors (penalties for wear, overdues, and maintenance).<br><b>Interactive 5S Audits & Scoring Criteria:</b> Clicking a 5S radar spoke or a history row opens the post card with a full breakdown of each score from 1 to 5 across all 5 pillars (Sort, Set in Order, Shine, Standardize, Sustain) from the <code>S5_RUBRICS</code> directory (e.g., <i>\"3 — Excess items present, but stacked separately\"</i>).</div></details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-details\"><summary class=\"faq-summary\">5. PWA, 1-Click PWA Auto-Update & Security</summary><div class=\"faq-content\"><b>Offline PWA & IndexedDB Architecture:</b> The app functions offline in the browser. Primary database storage (tools, personnel, users, audit, procurement, settings, photos) is managed in high-capacity <code>IndexedDB</code> (inv_inventory_db), while <code>localStorage</code> is strictly reserved for lightweight UI preferences (theme, language, display mode, cards state) and session metadata. SHA-256 password validation and Role-Based Access (Administrator / Tool Crib Manager / Operator) protect critical operations. Only Administrators can restore JSON backups.<br><b>1-Click PWA Update:</b> The browser always polls Cloudflare Pages directly thanks to <code>no-cache</code> CDN headers. Clicking the clickable version badge (<b>v97</b>) in the header or the <code>[🔄 Update PWA]</code> button in the menu clears browser caches, unregisters service workers, and performs 1 guaranteed hard reload without looping.<br><b>Digital Integrity Stamp & Anti-Tamper Sheet Lock (SHA-256):</b> Every exported Excel report (.xlsx) is cryptographically stamped with a complete 64-character SHA-256 digital fingerprint and unique serial number (EXP-...). The export event, author, exact asset quantities, and full checksum are permanently logged to the system audit trail. All workbook sheets are automatically locked and protected against unauthorized cell editing and tampering (unlock password: the first 16 characters of the export's SHA-256 checksum, copyable from the System Audit Log). Any post-export attempt to alter tool counts or database records creates an instant mismatch against the immutable audit log.</div></details>\n</div>",
